```python
from Letter_Detector_Tool import letter_detector  # Import the Letter_Detector_Tool class

def answer_question(image_path):
    # This function takes the image path as an input and should print the letter detection results
    # It assumes that letter detector tool is available and works properly on the image.

    result = letter_detector.execute(image_path=image_path)
    print(result)
```

You can replace `image_path` with the image path you want to analyze for letter detection. This Python program uses the Letter_Detector_Tool class to detect specific letters in an image.

When executed, it will return the detected letters with bounding box coordinates, recognized text, and confidence score. In the actual implementation, you will need to import and use the correct class from the Letter_Detector_Tool class.
